- `action(n14, "Start homework assignment")`: Has no outgoing `precedence` link, breaking the required iteration described as "If it was not the last homework, another homework assignment will be given."
- `precedence(n25, n27)` and `precedence(n27, e2)`: Routes the exam failure path directly to termination instead of cycling back to sign-up/attendance, contradicting "if the exam is failed, another sign-up for the exam is required."
- `action(n7, "Request exception again")`: Lacks an outgoing `precedence` statement, creating a dead-end branch unsupported by the description, which only specifies continuation after approval.
- `end(e1)` and `end(e2)`: Defines two termination points, violating the single intended progression where the process concludes only after passing; the failure path incorrectly terminates rather than looping.
- `branch(b1)`, `branch(b3)`, and `branch(b4)`: Lack corresponding `guard` statements linking to `v1`, `v3`, and `v4`, failing to explicitly encode the conditions "if an exception is needed", "if it was not the last homework", and "if the exam is passed/failed".
- `defines(v1, ...)`, `defines(v3, ...)`, and `defines(v4, ...)`: Declared with empty ranges `{}`, which do not faithfully reflect the binary decision nature implied by the conditional questions in the source text.
- `action(n18, "Merge accreditation and exam date announcement")` and `action(n26)/action(n27, "End")`: Hallucinates distinct process steps not documented in the description, which only describes concurrent tasks followed directly by exam sign-up and conceptual completion upon passing.

